TNT 2.0.0-rc2 - Linux release candidate
=====================================

Only Linux. This is a release candidate, not a final stable release.
No Windows version is provided.

Debian 12 / Ubuntu 24.04 / Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm or newer:
  dpkg --print-architecture
  sudo apt install ./tnt_2.0.0-rc2-1_arm64.deb
Use the matching amd64, arm64 or armhf file.
armhf requires ARMv7 hard-float: Pi 2 and newer with a 32-bit OS.
It is NOT compatible with the original Pi 1, Zero or Zero W (ARMv6).
arm64 requires a 64-bit OS; CPU capability alone does not determine the package.

openSUSE Leap 16 x86_64:
  sudo zypper install ./tnt-2.0.0-rc2-1.x86_64.rpm
The RPM is built/tested on Leap 16, NOT a universal Fedora/RHEL/openSUSE RPM.
Package metadata uses 2.0.0~rc2 for correct ordering before stable 2.0.0.
Download filenames use 2.0.0-rc2 because GitHub rewrites tilde characters.
Packages are not cryptographically signed; SHA256SUMS detects corruption,
but is not a substitute for an independently trusted signature.

Installation does not start TNT or change a running process, create a service,
or replace /usr/local/bin/tnt, ~/.local/bin/tnt or existing tnt.ini files.
The packaged programs are /usr/bin/tnt and /usr/bin/tntc.
Check "command -v tnt": older private installations may take precedence.
Upgrades do not restart sessions. Stop TNT cleanly before deliberately switching.

FIRST CONFIGURATION
RC2 defaults to the extended channel status line with database names
(altstat 1). Existing configurations retain their explicit altstat setting;
altstat 0 selects the classic display. Changing it requires restarting TNT.
RC2 also fixes LOADPRIV on existing connections, delayed callsign/name/status
updates, and failed LOADSYS/LDBLCMD reloads. See BUILD.md for details.

Example files are installed as /etc/tnt/*.ex; they are not active tnt.ini files.
The historical interactive setup is available as:
  sudo tnt_setup.de
It requires dialog and writes system configuration after your choices.
Do not run setup over an existing installation without a backup.
The French and English scripts are tnt_setup.fr and tnt_setup.en.
Configure your own hostmode TNC or TNN connection, callsign and file permissions.
Serial access usually requires membership in the distribution's dialout group;
log in again after changing group membership. Do not chmod a serial device 777.

For an EXISTING node/terminal, retain its config and working directory.
After backup and clean shutdown, test the packaged binary explicitly:
  /usr/bin/tnt -i /absolute/path/to/your/tnt.ini
Do not copy the example .ex files over your active configuration.
Read BUILD.md for updating termcap.tnt terminal profiles and UTF-8 locales.
The packaged terminal supports at most 256 columns and needs at least 80x16.

Important behavior change: UMLAUT ON now means ae/oe/ue/ss transliteration.
UMLAUT OFF (default) retains umlauts. Radio/file data remain legacy encoded;
UTF-8 conversion happens only at the terminal boundary.
Local resize and mouse channel switching are not enabled for tntc clients.

BUILD.txt identifies the repository, exact commit and target.
The release SOURCE archive / source RPM provides matching complete sources.
Debian ARM programs are cross-built and tested with QEMU, not every Pi model.
No live Pi/XP installation is modified by publishing these packages.
Use the separate SHA256SUMS file to check downloads before installation.
